	(descr "Amphenol LTW 8-03PMMP-SF7001, M8 A-coded 3-pole MALE receptacle, unshielded, STRAIGHT (180deg) PCB THT, PCB parallel to the panel, mounted from inside (Amphenol 'front fastened': housing and hex 10 flange behind the panel, M8x1 thread through it, O-ring on the inner face, flat nut from outside), panel 3.0 mm max, IP67, 3 A 60 V DC per contact, LCSC C21957007. Drawing 8-03PMMP-SF7001 rev D (2013-01-24): 3x D1.0 holes for D0.8 tails, 1 and 3 at 3.50, 4 offset 1.75 (contacts on a D3.5 circle around the axis); tails 3.0 below the seating face. Contact numbering from the front view (3 left, 1 right, 4 below the 1-3 line); tails are straight in line with the contacts, so the component-side view equals the front view. The board rests on the housing (D8.6); hex flange 2.56-4.40 above the PCB, O-ring seat (flange front) 4.40, O-ring to 5.87, mating face 16.4. Panel cut-out on Dwgs.User: D8.1 +/-0.1 with two flats 7.1 +0.1/-0 across, normal to the 1-3 line (thread flats read on the two side views). 3D model generated from the drawing (scripts/generate_8-03pmmp-sf7001.py): the Amphenol STEP could not be downloaded on 2026-11-11. Footprint origin = connector axis. https://amphenolltw.com/product-info/M-Series/M-Series.M8/8-03PMMP-SF7001.html")
	(tags "M8 A-coding receptacle male 3 pin straight vertical 180deg PCB panel sensor Amphenol LTW IP67 RS485")
